% INTRODUCTION, bars 1-6 (Adagio, 3/4). Concert pitch; Cb and Cbsn at sounding pitch.
% Common-tone link from movement I: its last chord (C major, C5 on top in Vln I, E natural only in the violas)
% turns to A flat major. The C stays on top; the violas' E falls to E flat; the cellos fall C to A flat.
% c010: bar 1 at ppp (movement I ends ppp); the moving voices reach pp at 2 while the common tone C stays (A&S PDF 585-587).
% c010: clarinets an octave lower at 3-6, so horn 3's C4-D flat4-C4 is the top voice: the common tone and its plagal neighbour stay exposed (A&S PDF 587).
% Bars 3-6: the winds take the chord over (strings out), with the plagal neighbour C-D flat-C in horn 3.

% c245: movement I (its v252) plays the last motto sul D at I 177-182, so the C5 tied into bar 1 is on the D string; the reminder runs to the end of the note
% (Gould PDF 21: every stave restates what governs it; PDF 23: nothing changes during a tied note), as movement I's own sul A spanners (tTwo.ily)
% c368: MIDI only: bar 3's niente diminuendo is on notes tied from 1-2, which keep their attack velocity; CC11 0.85 at 3 b1 and 0.6 at 3 b3 (a column the timpani already have, so spacing is unchanged), back to 1.0 at 4 (Casanelles PDF 124, 142: a sounding note's dynamic needs a continuous controller; PDF 142, Fig. 4.5: the release is part of the note). Vln I and II share a channel and fade together
introVlnOne = { \once \override TextSpanner.bound-details.left.text = \markup \italic "(sul D)" \once \override TextSpanner.bound-details.right.text = \markup \draw-line #'(0 . -1) \once \override TextSpanner.bound-details.right.padding = #5 c''2.\repeatTie~\ppp^\markup \italic "change bow at will" \startTextSpan | c''2.~ | \once \override Staff.Hairpin.circled-tip = ##t << c''2.\> \tag #'score { \set Staff.midiExpression = #0.85 s2 \set Staff.midiExpression = #0.6 s4 } >> | \set Staff.midiExpression = #1.0 R2.\!\stopTextSpan -\tag #'score ^\markup \small \italic "mettere sord. (not the solo player)" -\tag #'part -\tweak self-alignment-X #LEFT ^\markup \small \italic "mettere sord. (not the solo player)" | R2.*2 | }
introVlnTwo = { g'2.\repeatTie\ppp | aes'2.~\pp | \once \override Staff.Hairpin.circled-tip = ##t << aes'2.\> \tag #'score { \set Staff.midiExpression = #0.85 s2 \set Staff.midiExpression = #0.6 s4 } >> | \set Staff.midiExpression = #1.0 R2.\!^\markup \small \italic "mettere sord." | R2.*2 | }
% c305: repeat tie raised clear of the natural (Gould PDF 55: no characters collide)
introVla = { e'2.-\tweak extra-offset #'(0 . 0.9) \repeatTie\ppp | es'2.~\pp | \once \override Staff.Hairpin.circled-tip = ##t << es'2.\> \tag #'score { \set Staff.midiExpression = #0.85 s2 \set Staff.midiExpression = #0.6 s4 } >> | \set Staff.midiExpression = #1.0 R2.\!^\markup \small \italic "mettere sord." | R2.*2 | }
introVc = { c2.\repeatTie\ppp | aes,2.~\pp | \once \override Staff.Hairpin.circled-tip = ##t << aes,2.\> \tag #'score { \set Staff.midiExpression = #0.85 s2 \set Staff.midiExpression = #0.6 s4 } >> | \set Staff.midiExpression = #1.0 R2.\!^\markup \small \italic "mettere sord." | R2.*2 | }  % c208: advance mute warning where the strings stop (Adler part 1 PDF 60: time to put mutes on; MOLA PDF 5, Ex. 5: change marked where the player stops, as "via sord." at 31 and Hn 3-4 "mettere sord." at 82)
introCb = { R2. | aes,,2.\pp~-\tweak extra-spacing-width #'(0 . 0) -\tweak extra-spacing-height #'(-inf.0 . +inf.0) ^\markup \italic "change bow at will" | \once \override Staff.Hairpin.circled-tip = ##t << aes,,2.\> \tag #'score { \set Staff.midiExpression = #0.85 s2 \set Staff.midiExpression = #0.6 s4 } >> | \set Staff.midiExpression = #1.0 R2.\! | R2.*2 | }  % c196: the basses hold A flat1 for six beats (about 7 s) in one tie, pp to niente; the bass bow is "thicker, heavier, and quite a bit shorter", so a lengthy tenuto is marked change bow at will (Adler part 1 PDF 108), as at 61, 65-70 and 83-92

% c140: since movement I's cycle 140 (v160 on) horn 3 enters at its bar 181, so it holds C4 for two bars of Lento, the second under a fermata
% (about 13 s at ppp) before this bar; the c030 relief below is kept (no change of sound).
% c030: horn 3 has held C4 since movement I bar 180 (three bars of Lento and a fermata, about 18 s at ppp); tied on to bar 4 it
% would be over 30 s in one breath. Horn 4 enters under the tie on bar 1 beat 2 and carries the C4 through bar 2, horn 3 breathes
% in bar 2 and takes the C again at 3, so horn 3 stays on top at 3-6 (c010) and the sounding pitches are unchanged.
% c305: horn 3's repeat tie up (upper part; it collided with the ppp below; Gould PDF 52, 55)
introHnThree = { c'2^\repeatTie\ppp r4 | R2. | \partCombineChords c'2.~(\pp | c'2. | des'2. | c'2) r4 \partCombineAutomatic | }  % c125: 3-6 as one-stem chords (Gould PDF 60: same-duration notes share a stem; PDF 61: one stem direction through the phrase); the tie on horn 3's C alone split 3-4 into two voices  % c328: slur C4-D flat4-C4 so the neighbour figure is soft-tongued on one breath, as its muted echo at 87-90 (c188; Adler part 1 PDF 309, Ex. X-24; PDF 307, Ex. X-17)
% c125: in chord mode the part-combiner gave horn 4's re-struck A flat3 at 3 a tie as well; c280 ties horn 4 itself, so this stencil is no longer used
hnFourNoTie = #(lambda (grob) (let* ((nh (ly:spanner-bound grob LEFT)) (p (ly:event-property (event-cause nh) 'pitch))) (if (and (ly:pitch? p) (= (ly:pitch-notename p) 5)) #f (ly:tie::print grob))))
introHnFour = { r4 c'2~\ppp-\tag #'score _\markup \bold "4." |  % c045: label the second player's entry on the shared staff, as "3." labels the first (MOLA Ex. 6, PDF 11: players named on paired staves)
  c'2.\< \breathe | aes2.~\pp | aes2.~ | aes2.~ | aes2 r4 | }  % c280: A flat3 tied 3-6 (was re-struck each bar; MIDI held 3-4 only): the pedal is held as movement I holds it (Hn 4 A flat3 tied at I 73-76, the same chord; last chord tied into our bar 1); Adler part 2 PDF 192, seams do not show  % c166: breath before the A flat3 (horn 3 retakes the C4 at 3, Vln I still holds C5); 1 b2-6 b2 was about 18.5 s in one breath (Rimsky-Korsakov PDF 37, 44)
% c060: clarinet 1 rests at 3-6: its A flat3 was a unison with horn 4 (c030 relief) for four bars (Sebesky PDF 12-13, Ex. 1: economy;
% the lower-middle register lightened so horn 3's C-D flat-C, the preview of the plagal close, stays the focus, PDF 13-14). Was aes2.\pp | aes2. | aes2. | aes2 r4
introClOne = { R2.*6 | }
introClTwo = { R2.*2 | es2.~\pp | es2. | fes2. | es2 r4 | }  % c280: E flat3 tied 3-4 under horn 3's tied C4 (one held chord until the F flat at 5)
introBassCl = { R2.*2 | aes,2.~\pp | aes,2.~ | aes,2.~ | aes,2 r4 | }  % c280: A flat2 pedal tied 3-6 (about 12.7 s at crotchet = 52, pp)
introTimp = {
  << R2. { s2.^\markup \small \column { "Timp. in G, A♭, C, E♭ (as in movement I)" "soft sticks" } } >> | aes,2.:32\ppp~ | \once \override Staff.Hairpin.circled-tip = ##t aes,2:32\>~ aes,8\! r8 | R2.^\markup \small \italic "damp" | R2.^\markup \small \column { "muta G in A♭, A♭ in C, C in D♭" "(A♭ C D♭ E♭, low to high)" } | R2. |  % c566: "damp" at 4 before the muta at 5: the 28" drum rolled A flat2 at 2-3 and the bass clarinet holds the same A flat2 at 3-6, so the head would still ring when pedalled up to C3 (Adler part 2 PDF 80: show how long a note may ring; as the damps at 53, 62 and 86)  % c270: chain muta, each drum in range (Adler part 2 PDF 79, Ex. XII-46: 30" D2-A2, 28" F2-C3, 25" B♭2-F3, 23" D3-A3). Movement I tunes G 30", A♭ 28" (its A♭ drum goes to B♭2 and B2), C 25", E♭ 23"; "G in D♭" asked the 30" drum for D♭3, a fourth above its top A2. Now 30" A♭2, 28" C3, 25" D♭3, 23" E♭3, which is the drum order the scherzo label (A♭→E2, C→G2, D♭→B2, E♭→E3) and bar 92 assume.  % c056: tuning and sticks before the first note; roll ends on a tied stroke (Adler part 2 PDF 80-81, Ex. XII-47, XII-51; PDF 88 beaters)
}
% The horn's pickup into the theme (bar 7).
introHnOne = { R2.*5 | r2 \set Staff.soloText = "1. solo" es8(\p-\tag #'score ^\markup \italic "dolce espr." -\tag #'part ^\markup \italic "solo, dolce espr." f8 | }  % c035: one label, "1. solo", instead of "1." plus "solo"

% c040/c045: movement I's last harp chord (C2-G2-C3) is now damped in movement I at its bar 182 ("étouffez with Cb."), so movement II has no étouffez.
introHarpL = { R2.*6-\tag #'part _\markup \small \line { \italic "set pedals during the rests:" \harp-pedal #"^-^|^--^" } | }  % c116: starting setting in the part (Adler part 1 PDF 112); mid-movement changes stay score-only (c075, MOLA PDF 5)  % c076: no scordatura: bar 9 D flat is D flat2 (Rimsky-Korsakov PDF 46: extreme notes only in special circumstances and for octave doubling)  % c050: retune during 1-6; movement I runs attacca into bar 1, so there is no pause between movements (Rimsky-Korsakov PDF 21, axiom II)
